<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- CORRECTED 2026-09-08 after extracting and inspecting a real shipped sibling
	     project's IPA (Sudachi v0.0.1.7, another yuzu-derived iOS Switch emulator,
	     GPL-licensed like this one -- codesign -d --entitlements against its actual
	     binary, not documentation or a guess): its ENTIRE entitlements set is
	     get-task-allow + the two kernel.* keys below (plus auto-injected
	     application-identifier/team-identifier). It has NO allow-jit, NO
	     disable-executable-page-protection, NO dynamic-codesigning entitlement at all.

	     Those three keys this file previously carried are macOS Hardened Runtime
	     entitlements (com.apple.security.cs.*) -- they have no defined meaning on iOS
	     and were very likely doing nothing here, cargo-culted from macOS guidance.
	     Removed. get-task-allow is what actually matters: it's what a development/
	     ad-hoc-signed build (Xcode direct-to-device, or a sideloading tool's re-sign)
	     carries, and it's what makes the kernel treat the process as debuggable
	     (CS_DEBUGGED), which is the real, if still only partially confirmed, path to
	     mmap(MAP_JIT) succeeding on iOS -- see cemu-ios-muffin's own device test
	     (CS_DEBUGGED set, mprotect(R+X) succeeded, mmap(MAP_JIT) still refused with
	     errno 22) for the caveat that CS_DEBUGGED alone has been insufficient
	     elsewhere. Added the two kernel entitlements Sudachi's real profile carries --
	     extended-virtual-addressing and increased-memory-limit -- since a Switch
	     emulator's large guest-address-space mappings are a plausible reason a
	     memory-mapping call could fail independent of the JIT question entirely, and
	     this project didn't have them before.

	     Still true: whether any of this actually works depends on how whatever tool
	     signs/re-signs this app handles entitlement injection, which this repo doesn't
	     control, and this remains the top-priority open, device-only-testable question
	     for this project -- see STATUS.md. -->
	<key>get-task-allow</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.developer.kernel.extended-virtual-addressing</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.developer.kernel.increased-memory-limit</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
